## ✅ Replica Set (Very Simple English)

>**Replica set means MongoDB keeps the same data in more than one server. One server is main and others are backup. If the main server goes down, MongoDB automatically makes a backup server as main, so the application does not stop.**

---

## ✅ Sharding (Very Simple English)

> **Sharding means MongoDB splits big data into small parts and stores them in different servers. This helps the database work faster and handle large data without load on one server.**


## ⭐ Combined Answer (You can say this together)

> **MongoDB uses replica sets to keep backup of data and avoid application downtime if one server fails. MongoDB uses sharding to divide large data across multiple servers so the system becomes fast and scalable.**

> **Replica set keeps same data in many servers for safety. Sharding splits data into many servers for speed. MongoDB does all this automatically.**
